# Design System Principles

## Core Rule

**Design system > Pixel Perfect.**

Figma mockups are a guide, not a blueprint. The designer can make mistakes: use the wrong token, set the wrong spacing, forget about another theme. The design system is the contract. The mockup is an illustration.

## Hierarchy of Authority

```
1. Design tokens (42 tokens in PaletteTokens)     ← HIGHEST
2. Spacing scale (Tailwind 4px grid)
3. Component API contracts (Props interfaces)
4. Figma mockups                                   ← REFERENCE ONLY
```

If a mockup contradicts the design system — **the design system wins**.

## Rules

### 1. Colors: ONLY tokens

```tsx
// ✅ Design system token
<div className="bg-card-bg text-text-primary" />

// ❌ Color from Figma screenshot
<div className="bg-[#373737] text-[#ffffff]" />

// ❌ Even if Figma shows exactly this color
// Tokens adapt to palette + dark/light mode. Hardcoded colors don't.
```

If a mockup uses a color that doesn't match any token:
1. Check if it's a mistake (most common) — use the closest token
2. If it's intentionally new — add a new token to `PaletteTokens` + all palettes

### 2. Spacing: Tailwind scale, not pixel values from Figma

```tsx
// ✅ Use Tailwind spacing (4px grid)
<div className="p-4 gap-2 mt-6" />   // 16px, 8px, 24px

// ❌ Exact Figma pixel value
<div className="p-[13px] gap-[7px]" />  // Not on 4px grid

// Exception: design-critical exact values (sidebar width: 299px → token)
```

Tailwind spacing scale: 0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3, 3.5, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 20, 24...
(0px, 2px, 4px, 6px, 8px, 10px, 12px, 14px, 16px, 20px, 24px, 32px, 40px, 48px, 56px, 64px, 80px, 96px...)

If Figma shows 13px padding → round to `p-3` (12px) or `p-3.5` (14px).

### 3. Typography: scale, not arbitrary sizes

```tsx
// ✅ Tailwind type scale
<p className="text-sm" />     // 14px
<p className="text-base" />   // 16px
<p className="text-lg" />     // 18px

// ❌ Arbitrary size from Figma
<p className="text-[15px]" />
```

### 4. Border radius: tokens

```tsx
// ✅ Consistent radius
<div className="rounded-lg" />    // 16px (our token)
<div className="rounded-full" />  // pills, badges, avatars

// ❌ Figma-specific radius
<div className="rounded-[14px]" />
```

### 5. Shadows, opacity: from design system

Use Tailwind shadow/opacity utilities. If Figma has custom shadow — check if an existing utility matches before adding `shadow-[custom]`.

### 6. Icons: from the icon registry

Always use `<Icon name="..." />` from `shared/ui/icon.tsx`. Don't inline SVGs from Figma.

## When Mockup and System Disagree

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Figma uses a color not in tokens | Use closest token; report to designer |
| Figma spacing is off-grid (13px) | Round to nearest 4px grid value |
| Figma font size is non-standard | Use nearest Tailwind scale step |
| Figma shows dark theme only | Implement for both dark AND light |
| Figma shows one palette only | Ensure works with ALL registered palettes |
| Figma component differs from existing | Prefer existing component; extend if needed |
| Figma shows different border radius | Use `rounded-lg` (16px) or `rounded-full` |

## Validation Checklist

Before marking UI work as done:
- [ ] All colors are semantic tokens (no `[#hex]`)
- [ ] All spacing on 4px grid (no `[Npx]` except defined tokens)
- [ ] Works in dark mode
- [ ] Works in light mode
- [ ] Works with Orange Warm palette
- [ ] Works with Blue Cold palette
- [ ] Text readable in all theme variants
- [ ] Accent colors from tokens, not hardcoded
- [ ] Icons from `<Icon>` registry

## For AI Agent

When implementing UI from a Figma screenshot:
1. Identify the INTENT of the design (layout, hierarchy, spacing rhythm)
2. Map to existing tokens and components
3. DO NOT match exact pixel values — match the design system
4. If a new token is needed, propose it — don't hardcode
5. Always test both themes and both palettes mentally
